<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE DOV. A hidden, permanently hostile faction that exists for exactly one reason:
  SO THAT DRAGONS CAN BE HOSTILE WITHOUT BEING IN A MENTAL STATE.

  ============================================================================================
  WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL
  ============================================================================================
  Dragons were made hostile with ManhunterPermanent, because a factionless animal is hostile to
  nobody (this project's own long-standing gotcha). That worked, and it cost everything else:
  MENTAL STATES OUTRANK LordDuty IN THE ANIMAL THINK TREE, so while a dragon was manhunting, no
  duty we set could ever run. The attack-pattern executor could choose his STATE - sprite and
  speed - while the manhunter AI did the actual fighting. The user, after three playtests:
  "he still acts very much like a wild beast", "doesn't circle around at all and just chases and
  kills like any normal manhunting beast".

  Hostility from a FACTION instead of a mental state frees the duty branch, and the patterns can
  finally own his behaviour rather than decorate it.

  ============================================================================================
  SHAPED AFTER VANILLA'S OWN "Insect" FACTION (Core/Factions_Hidden.xml)
  ============================================================================================
  Hidden, non-humanlike, animal tech, permanently hostile, no diplomacy, no settlements, and a
  raid commonality curve pinned to zero so the storyteller can never send a dragon raid on its
  own. Dragons arrive because this mod spawns them, never because RimWorld decided to.

  ⚠ requiredCountAtGameStart is 0, NOT 1 like Insect's. A faction with a required count is
  created at world generation - which does nothing for the SAVES THAT ALREADY EXIST, and this
  project is being tested on one. DovahFactionUtility creates the instance on demand instead, so
  it works on an existing save and on a new one identically.
-->
<Defs>

  <FactionDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DovFaction</defName>
    <label>dov</label>
    <description>The dov - dragons. Firstborn of Akatosh, and older than men. They do not treat, they do not trade, and they do not forgive; a dragon that speaks to you is deciding how you will die.</description>
    <pawnSingular>dovah</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>dov</pawnsPlural>
    <fixedName>The Dov</fixedName>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>0</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <canMakeRandomly>false</canMakeRandomly>

    <humanlikeFaction>false</humanlikeFaction>
    <hidden>true</hidden>
    <permanentEnemy>true</permanentEnemy>
    <techLevel>Animal</techLevel>

    <!-- A dovah does not run away. SPEC.md 6.5: below half health he STAYS GROUNDED and fights,
         which is what makes him killable at all - fleeing would make that rule meaningless. -->
    <autoFlee>false</autoFlee>
    <canUseAvoidGrid>false</canUseAvoidGrid>

    <!-- Pinned to zero: the storyteller must never raise a dragon raid from this faction.
         Dragons appear through this mod's own events, per ROADMAP Phase 3. -->
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>

    <!-- ⚠ REQUIRED WHENEVER raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve IS DEFINED. RimWorld's own config
         check says so in as many words - "raidLootValueFromPointsCurve must be defined" - and it
         is a RED error at load, which CLAUDE.md forbids leaving in place.
         Zero throughout: dragons carry no loot and this faction never raids anyway. Another case
         of the notebook's standing rule - a clean build and a def that PARSES both pass this;
         only RimWorld's load-time config pass catches it. -->
    <raidLootValueFromPointsCurve>
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0)</li>
      </points>
    </raidLootValueFromPointsCurve>

    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.36, 0.13, 0.10)</li>
      <li>(0.55, 0.22, 0.13)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
  </FactionDef>

</Defs>
